      "scope_note": "The four original picture tickets now have a **repaired, native-regenerated source candidate saved in full**, with a fresh full source gate and code PR still pending. This is the closed source02 snapshot, staged as `0d82fa9b2e7beb744089c70a53cb66cb1a0ffd7f` on HEAD `02e303c2188e4a4a32fb807a28e9b07d78a8c23d`. It remains uncommitted work. Checkpoint754's earlier `c362380a` candidate and its7/1,109 failed full gate remain failed; none of the newer focused results is relabeled as that full gate passing.\n\nAll **111 changed source postimages (102,844,714 bytes)** were exported under root authorization into `next-four-repaired-02-stage0d82-source-postimages-CLOSED-20261031`. Every file's size, SHA256, Git blob, Git executable mode and filesystem mode was checked against the closed stage result, copied externally, then verified against the source in a second pass. No Git command, source/index/ref/config write or further live-source read was used for the export. This complete snapshot preserves the unique native terrain binaries as well as repaired source and generated metadata, rather than requiring another agent to reconstruct them from scattered historical prefixes.\n\nFor exact restoration, check out canonical02 and overlay the111 repository-relative files from the closed capsule with their recorded bytes/modes. Other canonical02 leaves remain from that commit. The closed stage result and source map identify the intended tree; ordinary explicit staging can recreate it, but this does not qualify it for shipping. Later current-dev integration, actual bridge-walk output, fresh full gates, runtime/phone/CI or code-PR work are outside this checkpoint and must be checked separately before reuse.\n\nRoot applied the authored liberty/context, Photos-contract alias and placement/corridor corrections. The rights and placement baselines were regenerated by their native owners. Ten focused pre-terrain native commands passed, including the associated rejection self-tests. After terrain work, `python3 tools/validate.py --all` reported0 errors and299 warnings. These are specific focused checks; no warning-free dataset or complete1,109-step source pass is claimed.\n\nThe actual terrain repair was generated by real Blender/native commands, not a heightfield or receipt patch. V3 completed nine native commands covering the two epoch producers, four WEB derivatives,1812 overlay controls, vertical/horizontal fits and derivative contracts, with all processes reaped. The full bridge end-edge measurement fell to **0.061538 m** worst gap, below the previous roughly0.71 m gap. The1812/natural physical heightfield and river controls remained byte-exact; its native receipt/master serialization changed during the real rebuild. The saved111 files include both new terrain masters, WEB products and changed field/meta data. Bridge model/camera projection changes are not attributed to this terrain operation. A fresh actual application walk is not claimed here.\n\nThe earlier V2 native command ran, but its external inputs-receipt assertion failed before completing the derivative/fit chain. Its exact output, reapers and launch traceback are retained as an unqualified partial attempt. V3's separately pinned controller and actual production checks supply the completed evidence; V2 is not promoted to a completed pass.\n\nThe repaired native-owner chain then completed **135 actual native commands**, including two61-command laps. The first lap updated the expected source/terrain/yard/coverage outputs and workbook serialization; the second changed no repository path, with identical complete before/after snapshots. Every recorded step returned exit0 with children reaped and no leftover cleanup. The later explicit stage preserved raw/native workbook evidence, proved full XML/payload equivalence and restored only canonical02 serialization. This native convergence is distinct from a fresh full source gate or browser/mobile/phone result.\n\nThe four existing claims were renewed through native ticket tooling as commit `157c4b9a20713e9b139261d58b1ab552d6cc469d`, with verified existing ownership, no rival override and immutable remote readback. T-2372, T-2375, T-2378 and T-2382 remain claimed, not done; no application code commit, PR or merge is asserted. The live image gallery/PR15 evidence stays in754, and the PR1486/T-3262 completed user-merge correction stays in753.\n\nContinue with the separately closed actual bridge/desktop/mobile and phone checks, current-dev integration as needed, the fresh full native source gate, checked code commits, PRs and normal merges into dev. Do not treat the old failed tree or an organizational prefix plan as gated. Every shell should source `/workspace/shared/resume-chicago-env.sh`. All previous archives and recovery history remain preserved; active later outputs and TMP/profile trees are excluded. This archive uses root-requested4 MiB raw lossless parts, normal force:false publication and complete immutable part/member verification.",
